WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.870
Crypto moves fast.

2
00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:03.630
Everyone buys at the top.

3
00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.510
Everyone panics at the bottom.

4
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:06.770
People do not lose because

5
00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.390
they picked the wrong coin.

6
00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:11.790
They lose because they decided with their feelings.

7
00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:12.910
This is the long version

8
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.030
of how Strategya fixes that.

9
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.840
Where the strategies come from,

10
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:17.870
what a card is,

11
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.150
how to read the Catalog and the Summary,

12
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.410
how to choose a plan,

13
00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:22.420
and how to follow a

14
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.550
card by hand or automatically.

15
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.910
Take eight minutes.

16
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.070
After this, the site has no secrets.

17
00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.990
Start with the one idea behind everything.

18
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.360
You need a strategy,

19
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.470
a rule, written down before the market moves,

20
00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.710
that says when to be in

21
00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.030
and when to be out.

22
00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.980
Not a feeling, not a tip,

23
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.990
not a chart you stare at all day.

24
00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.830
A rule you can test on years of

25
00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:47.750
data and follow without arguing with it.

26
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.070
Two sentences we use all the time.

27
00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.550
We don't predict, we react.

28
00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.950
The rule does not know where Bitcoin is going.

29
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.760
It waits for conditions to

30
00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.830
align and then it acts.

31
00:00:58.830 --> 00:00:59.860
And the second one,

32
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.550
it is not how much you make,

33
00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.750
it is how much you do not lose.

34
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.590
Capital you keep is capital that keeps compounding.

35
00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:10.590
Every number on this site is a simulated backtest.

36
00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.870
The rule applied to past prices with commission.

37
00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:17.230
Never real performance, never advice.

38
00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:19.190
A good rule is not magic.

39
00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.470
It is three things working together.

40
00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.250
Trend filters that adapt to how volatile the market

41
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.080
is so the rule is in the market only

42
00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.590
when the probabilities are in its favor and in

43
00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.390
cash the rest of the time.

44
00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.910
Volume confirmation.

45
00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:33.670
Price going up is not enough.

46
00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:35.840
There has to be real participation behind

47
00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.990
the move or there is no trade.

48
00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.950
And risk management, which is where most people fail.

49
00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.490
A fixed amount of capital,

50
00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.800
a stop outside the strategy and

51
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.950
no arguing with the rule.

52
00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.790
Our rules were tested across complete cycles.

53
00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:52.020
The COVID crash, two havings,

54
00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.750
the arrival of the ETFs,

55
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.990
bull markets and bear markets.

56
00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:58.950
They trade little, quality over quantity.

57
00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.030
Being out of the market is a decision too.

58
00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:05.350
Every Strategya rule was born in TradingView.

59
00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:06.990
This is what it looks like there.

60
00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.030
Green when the rule is in the market,

61
00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.410
red when it is out and

62
00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.230
the blue line is the money.

63
00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.870
It goes flat when the rule sits in cash.

64
00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.350
That flat part is not inactivity.

65
00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:18.950
It is protection.

66
00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.190
That is where we started.

67
00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.380
And for a while that is what we offered.

68
00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.630
A TradingView strategy you had to load,

69
00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.950
configure and watch yourself.

70
00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.910
Most people never got that far.

71
00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:31.110
TradingView is a professional tool,

72
00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.270
powerful and intimidating.

73
00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.430
So we did the work on our side.

74
00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.260
The same engine now runs every day

75
00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.570
after the close on our servers,

76
00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.950
checked against TradingView on every run

77
00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.860
and it publishes one thing,

78
00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:44.950
a card.

79
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.760
You never open a chart,

80
00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.150
you read the card.

81
00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.020
This is the Bitcoin card today,

82
00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.750
100% in cash waiting.

83
00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.530
It tells you whether it changed today,

84
00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.270
the last change with its date,

85
00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:58.130
the last trade with its result

86
00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.150
and the live price since then.

87
00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:01.390
One decision a day at

88
00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:03.170
the close of the candle.

89
00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.260
No charts, no TradingView,

90
00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.930
no trading background.

91
00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.870
This is built for everyone.

92
00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.470
Tap the plus and the full card opens.

93
00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:14.230
First, the strategy against simply holding.

94
00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:17.010
Same $1,000, same start date.

95
00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.710
Then max drawdown, the worst fall along the way.

96
00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:23.830
On Bitcoin, the rules is a fraction of holding.

97
00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:26.950
The position history, a ribbon of every day.

98
00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.210
The replay bar by bar,

99
00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.350
every trade on one line.

100
00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:33.970
And the statistics like a strategy tester

101
00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.550
with a window selector on every number.

102
00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.360
The guide has a four minute

103
00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.070
video just on this card.

104
00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.880
The Catalog is one card

105
00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:44.310
per strategy in three tiers.

106
00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.230
Entry is one strategy.

107
00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.630
Bitcoin, one decision a day.

108
00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:51.350
Intermediate is the whole long only line.

109
00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:54.110
Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana, SUI,

110
00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:58.230
Gold, Tesla, MicroStrategy and the rotations.

111
00:03:58.230 --> 00:03:59.560
Cards that choose every day

112
00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:02.270
between several assets or cash.

113
00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:05.210
Expert adds the long and short strategies

114
00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.110
which can also bet on a fall.

115
00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:10.470
They're in early access and the results are preliminary.

116
00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.280
Filter what you care about,

117
00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.170
sovereign or rotation, daily or 12 hour with shorts,

118
00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.390
with stocks.

119
00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.200
Within each tier, the cards are

120
00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.150
ordered by their last trade.

121
00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:24.550
The Summary puts all 23 strategies in one table,

122
00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.450
measured on the same window and ranked by

123
00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.430
MAR which is return divided by drawdown.

124
00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:31.460
Next to each one,

125
00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.590
the same three numbers for simply holding the asset.

126
00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.700
That is the benchmark and beating it is

127
00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.190
the only reason to run a strategy.

128
00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:41.170
Change the window, filter,

129
00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.510
sort by any column,

130
00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.490
hover the info icons for a plain English definition

131
00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.830
and open any card right there inside the table.

132
00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.790
Three plans, monthly.

133
00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.910
Each one including the ones below.

134
00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:55.470
Entry, $5, Bitcoin.

135
00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:59.710
Intermediate, 29, the 14 long only strategies.

136
00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.400
Expert, 59, adds the eight long

137
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.110
and short strategies in early access.

138
00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.100
Every plan includes the daily signal,

139
00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.540
the full card and the

140
00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.590
connector for your AI assistant.

141
00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:12.980
To get access, tap request access

142
00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:14.290
on the plan you want.

143
00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.510
It opens an email to us.

144
00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:19.060
A card says one of three things,

145
00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.310
in cash, long or short.

146
00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.120
A signal is a decision,

147
00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.390
not an execution.

148
00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.590
Nobody places an order for you.

149
00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:29.250
So what do you do with it? Three paths,

150
00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:30.250
by hand.

151
00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:32.140
After the close, read the card and

152
00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.390
place the order on your own exchange.

153
00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:37.980
With Signum, an execution platform where your exchange keys

154
00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:41.270
live and one bot per strategy places the orders.

155
00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.350
Or with your AI assistant.

156
00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:47.150
Connect the Strategya connector because Strategya speaks MCP.

157
00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.910
Ask it what the position is today.

158
00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:50.120
And if you want,

159
00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.750
schedule a routine that reads the signal and acts

160
00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:55.990
through Signum with the template on the automation page.

161
00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:57.870
The rules we use ourselves.

162
00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.680
Fixed capital per bot,

163
00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.710
an external stop on the exchange.

164
00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:04.230
Confirm the pair before every order.

165
00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.670
No reentry after a manual stop.

166
00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:09.400
An expired card is not a signal and

167
00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.410
keys never leave the exchange and Signum.

168
00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:14.270
That is the whole system.

169
00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.080
A rule born in TradingView,

170
00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.670
tested on years of data,

171
00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.560
run every day on our side and

172
00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.050
published as a card anyone can read.

173
00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:23.860
The guide has one short video for

174
00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.670
each page if you wanna go deeper.

175
00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.910
Everything here is a simulated backtest,

176
00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:31.030
not real performance and not investment advice.

177
00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.980
Pick your asset, check the card,

178
00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:34.470
decide once.

179
00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:37.420
Strategya.pro, we don't predict,

180
00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:38.800
we react.

